= The Stowford Front

The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> parties and paramilitaries - the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> (and its paramilitary the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>), the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> paramilitary group, and the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> - have united to form the Stowford Front, as a force dedicated to the overthrow of the current government. The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>, once aloof, are increasingly drawn to the Royalists' Imperial nostalgia—the old longing for the Empress's return doing what mere tactics could not. 

However, this show of unity lacks substance, as Mallin, Gallax, and the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> compete against one another to assert themselves as the leader of the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">national</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">opposition</span>. Gallax's erratic behavior—such as vanishing from the podium when <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> detachments march by—has offended many conservatives[? if bruning_time:, and inter-party polemics may only serve to reinforce Askew against their pressures?]. [? if gold_leader == "Coalfax" and gold_exist: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> has worryingly some sympathies towards the national opposition, with some members even attending or sending congratulatory telegrams. ?][? if bruning_time: Luckily, the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical":<span style="color: #0087DC;">**CPP**</span>?]'s Trevannon has dissuaded many influential guild-masters from taking part in this gathering ?]

